# CODING_STANDARDS.md

Applies to all application source code changes made by the Senior Developer role, in both FULL and
LIGHT mode. This document describes standards for this specific repository
(`{{PRIMARY_SOURCE_FILES}}`, architecture style: `{{ARCHITECTURE_STYLE}}`), not a generic style
guide — fill in the "Project-specific" sections below as the project accrues its own conventions
and defect history.

## General principles

- Match the existing code's conventions before introducing new ones. Do not fragment or
  restructure the codebase's file layout unless an approved architecture explicitly calls for it.
- Prefer the smallest change that correctly implements the approved scope (`02-ARCHITECTURE.md` in
  FULL mode, `LIGHT_CONTEXT.md` in LIGHT mode). Do not refactor unrelated code "while you're in
  there" — file it as a follow-up note instead.
- No behavior changes outside the current milestone's approved scope.

## Security (generic defaults — keep these regardless of stack)

- Never insert user- or API-controlled content into a rendering surface without escaping (e.g.
  `innerHTML` in a browser context, unsanitized template interpolation server-side, unparameterized
  SQL). Treat any new unescaped-interpolation pattern as a defect risk by default.
- Never commit API keys, tokens, or credentials into source. See `.ai-company/GIT_RULES.md`.
- Validate/handle deserialization and external-storage reads defensively (`JSON.parse`,
  `localStorage`, file reads, API responses) — corrupted or missing state should degrade
  gracefully, not throw or crash.

## Conventions

- Match existing naming and function style already present in `{{PRIMARY_SOURCE_FILES}}`.
- Guard against duplicate/overlapping async operations that mutate shared state (id collisions on
  rapid repeated actions, double-submit on slow network, race conditions on concurrent writes).
- Prefer explicit error/loading states over silent fallbacks that could be mistaken for real data.

## Comments and TODOs

- A deliberate no-op or deferred feature must have a TODO comment in the code stating what it does
  today and which milestone will address it — do not leave silent dead code.

## Scope discipline

- If implementing the approved scope reveals a necessary change outside its stated file list, stop
  and flag it (in `03-IMPLEMENTATION-LOG.md` or `LIGHT_CONTEXT.md`) and back to the CEO/Architect
  rather than expanding scope unilaterally. In LIGHT mode, a file outside `LIGHT_CONTEXT.md`'s
  allowed list is also a FULL-mode escalation trigger — see `.ai-company/MODE_SELECTION.md`.

